  "notes": "Common thresholds: medicate at ≥ 8–10, reassess q1h until < 8–10 for 8 h then space out. CIWA does NOT capture autonomic instability well — a patient with a normal-ish score but tachycardia, hypertension, and fever may still be decompensating. Give thiamine before glucose; replace magnesium, potassium, phosphate.",
